{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478486-deep-space-options-no-war-beyond-the-line","id":1478486,"title":"Deep Space Options \"No War Beyond the Line!\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-10T06:06:53-07:00","id":1478486,"title":"Deep Space Options \"No War Beyond the Line!\"","content":"Given that one of the main options for the Void Engineers is that they have bases and colonies in deep space and that many of their members were born off Earth and have little or no interest in visiting Earth, it seems to me this is a great option for Space Opera. It's been established that the Void Engineers are very tolerant of Council Mages and others when other members of the Union can't spy on them. <br /> <br /> An Horizon realm that is a planet in another star system with an Hermetic School (would you have enough people to be called a university?) an a multi Cabal Chantry might be approached by the Void Engineers who'd like to set a scout base there. You could blend pulp &quot;East of Suez&quot; adventure, with Golden Age Sci Fi, and several other types of adventure stories. <br /> <br /> If there is a division, but a peaceful one, in the ranks of the Void Engineers, with many of those living in deep space being far less committed to Earth, Trad Mages and Changelings might be seen as good recruits for deep space exploration.<br /> <br /> Picture a Void Engineer ship (looking a lot like the &quot;Enterprise&quot; or the &quot;Orville&quot;) many crewed by Void Engineers but with Etherians, Hermetics, VAs, Sidhe, Satyrs, ect, joining the mission. <br /> <br /> I for one, still want a Space Opera book.<br /> <br /> What Deep Space options do you like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T06:42:14-07:00","id":1478489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478486-deep-space-options-no-war-beyond-the-line#post1478486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that one of the main options for the Void Engineers is that they have bases and colonies in deep space and that many of their members were born off Earth and have little or no interest in visiting Earth, it seems to me this is a great option for Space Opera. It's been established that the Void Engineers are very tolerant of Council Mages and others when other members of the Union can't spy on them.<br /> <br /> An Horizon realm that is a planet in another star system with an Hermetic School (would you have enough people to be called a university?) an a multi Cabal Chantry might be approached by the Void Engineers who'd like to set a scout base there. You could blend pulp &quot;East of Suez&quot; adventure, with Golden Age Sci Fi, and several other types of adventure stories.<br /> <br /> If there is a division, but a peaceful one, in the ranks of the Void Engineers, with many of those living in deep space being far less committed to Earth, Trad Mages and Changelings might be seen as good recruits for deep space exploration.<br /> <br /> Picture a Void Engineer ship (looking a lot like the &quot;Enterprise&quot; or the &quot;Orville&quot;) many crewed by Void Engineers but with Etherians, Hermetics, VAs, Sidhe, Satyrs, ect, joining the mission.<br /> <br /> I for one, still want a Space Opera book.<br /> <br /> What Deep Space options do you like</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fun. I would personally suggest &quot;Ascension Truce&quot; metaplot for a Space Opera and if you truly want Babylon 5 style space opera, you can have a Space Station (or private planet/dimension/realm) built to symbolize the truce and have members from every Tradition and Convention. <br /> <br /> Changelings are not a good option though. all Technocrats are too Banal for them. (Even VA and SoE can be too much)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T11:10:24-07:00","id":1478502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478486-deep-space-options-no-war-beyond-the-line?p=1478489#post1478489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds fun. I would personally suggest &quot;Ascension Truce&quot; metaplot for a Space Opera and if you truly want Babylon 5 style space opera, you can have a Space Station (or private planet/dimension/realm) built to symbolize the truce and have members from every Tradition and Convention. </div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking a small scale place. I'm reading a book on Native American diplomacy in the Southeast during the American Revolution. So I'm thinking about small but highly cosmopolitan places on a frontier. But your idea is fun too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings are not a good option though. all Technocrats are too Banal for them. (Even VA and SoE can be too much) </div> </div> </div>As I see it, Deep Space is like the Far Dreaming for the Changelings. So they wouldn't be so vulnerable to Banality. The Changelings become a type of alien that the Void Engineers can deal with and ally with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T18:53:49-07:00","id":1480502,"title":"","content":"Anyone who's seen &quot;The Cage&quot; or read any of C.L.Moore's &quot;Northwest of Earth&quot; will get the deep links between Space Opera/Planetary Romance and Golden Age Sci Fi on one hand and the Arabian Nights on the other. This leads to a link between deep space and deep time that ties back to the Earth, Mount Qaf. <br /> <br /> Mt. Qaf is already established as a realm that the Batini regularly passed through as part of their mastery of Correspondence. Both folklore and White Wolf materials on the Djinni make Mt. Qaf the home of the Djinni. The City of Brass was originally on Mt. Qaf in Arab lore. <br /> <br /> All this would suggest that many of the planets that the Void Engineers and others would contact in deep space would be aspects of Mt. Qaf. After all, when you think of it Captain Kirk and Sinbad the Sailor tended to land in similar places. I have to wonder if they ran into Sir John Mandeville or Lemuel Gulliver on their travels. <br /> <br /> But assuming that deep space and the deep dreaming and the astral realms are all aspects of each other lets you use Sci Fi themes in very Magey ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T19:06:13-07:00","id":1480614,"title":"","content":"Who are the antagonists? It needs two or three main groups of antagonists. There could be raiders, intelligent predators, body snatchers, etcetera. <br /> <br /> Resources: You could take away Nodes completely to make the game more interesting. Have some resources be really abundant and others rare - the rare ones being of greatest Quintessence value.<br /> <br /> On this planet, and particularly near the Chantry, what is the climate like?<br /> <br /> There could be an economy built around the writing of Grimoires for the Magic University. The right to extend your lifespan has to be earned through great deeds in service to the colony.<br /> <br /> I would also have massive caves and tunnel complexes all over the planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T03:53:18-07:00","id":1480651,"title":"","content":"First for antagonists the Djinni themselves. They despise Mages. Since the Far Dreaming intersects with this place Unseelie Changelings and other fey creatures seem like viable threats. Although most of the Umbrood of this area of the Tapestry are simply alien, many are hostile and preditory. Some of the more alien Umbrood are functionally insane, not in the sense of an actual mental disorder but in the simple fact that they have no shared frame of reference with humans. The possibilities for conflict are vast. Lastly both nephandi and marauders would be threats as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T21:06:17-07:00","id":1480722,"title":"","content":"Using the Nephandi, one idea comes to mind. Destroying the colony would probably not be the goal of whichever demon-lord lurks out there. Since they are colonists from Earth, destroying the colony is like cutting off humanity's baby toe. It doesn't have the finality of destroying Earth. <br /> <br /> It might be in the interest of the Nephandi to encourage fertility, in order to increase the number of souls they could later devour. If the tecno-magic possessed by the colonists makes them a post scarcity society, the only thing that limits birthrates is choice. Nephandi agents in their midst could create a social system that accords status to couples who have the most children. <br /> <br /> Low intelligence Umbrood who sense the potential the colony has to serve as fuel for the demon-lord would instinctually attack the colony. Changelings could be drawn into the conflict in some way. Technophandi-Ironhands start churning out weapons that repel the attacking Umbrood by inflicting pain, but also make them more aggressive, post-recovery. As the adults become increasingly occupied with defense, the Ironhands also manufacture educational toy robots that become indispensable during the crisis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}